      "raw_response": "REFUTED\n\nThe Chagatai language, also known as Chagatai Turkish, was not the shared literary language of Central Asia. Instead, the Khwarezmian language was the primary literary language of Central Asia during the Chaghatai khanate period. This information is well-documented in historical sources such as \"The History of the World Conqueror\" by Rashid-al-Din Hamad ibn Qara, which explicitly mentions the use of Khwarezmian (a language related to modern Persian) in the region.\n\nANSWER: REFUTED",
