      "raw_response": " ANSWER: SUPPORTED\n\nThe Chagatai language was indeed a significant literary language in Central Asia, particularly during the Timurid period. This can be confirmed by various sources, including Wikipedia (as of 2017). The Timurid court, located in Samarkand, used Chagatai for official correspondence and literary works. Notable works such as the \"Chagatai Minhaj al-Syrin\" and the \"Chagatai Divan-i Lughat-i Turk\" further support its role as a literary language in the region.\n\nReference(s):\n- Wikipedia (2017): Chagatai language - https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chagatai_language\n- Encyclopaedia Iranica (2017): Chagatai Literature - https://www.iranicaonline.org/articles/chagatai-literature",
